<h1>Delete a study group</h1>
<p class="lead">
  Remove a group from the current session after confirming your choice.
</p>

<h2>Before you begin</h2>
<p>
  You need an existing group to delete. You can
  <a href="/features/create-group">create an example group</a>
  to practice this feature.
</p>

<h2>Step-by-step instructions</h2>
<ol>
  <li>On the main window, click <strong>Show all</strong>
      or filter the list to find your group.</li>
  <li>Click the group you want to remove to select it.</li>
  <li>Click <strong>Delete group</strong>.</li>
  <li>Read the confirmation dialog and check that you selected
      the intended group.</li>
  <li>To keep the group, click <strong>Cancel</strong>.
      To remove it, choose the dialog's confirmation option.</li>
  <li>After confirming, check the main list. The group is removed,
      and the displayed list and result count update.</li>
</ol>

<figure>
  <img src="/images/studyhub-delete.png"
       alt="StudyHub confirmation dialog displayed before deleting a selected study group">
  <figcaption>
    Review the confirmation before removing a group.
    Cancel keeps the group unchanged.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<h2>What to expect</h2>
<p>
  A group must be selected before it can be deleted.
  If you delete the last group matching your filters, the list
  displays its empty state.
</p>
<p>
  Deletion has no undo feature. If you remove a group by mistake,
  use <strong>Create group</strong> to enter its information again.
</p>

<aside class="notice">
  <strong>Local demonstration:</strong>
  This application has no accounts or group-leader authorization.
  Deletion affects only the groups in the current local session.
</aside>

